  "content": "{\n  \"feedback\": \"草稿与原文存在以下不匹配：1. 关键点1称“每秒十亿次计算‘可能差不多’”，原文为“a billion calculations per second is probably not far off”，意思接近但表述略有差异，不影响核心。2. 关键点2称“用 Python 的 random.randint 在 16 到 272 之间抽到编号 75”，原文为“choose a random number between 16 and 272”，但随后说“75”，并说“find the number in the responder's sheet”，编号75对应Lauren Z-O-V，表述一致。3. 关键点3称“该配方/算法有三部分：简单的步骤序列（四步）、带判断与重复的控制流，以及停止方式（如接近程度取 .01 或 .001）”，原文明确说“There were four steps.”和“Close enough was maybe being within .01, .001, whatever you pick.”，一致。4. 关键点5称“控制单元含一个程序计数器，从第一条指令开始，把指令送给 ALU，通常递增 1 到下一指令”，原文为“the program counter starts at the first sequence. It starts at the sequence, at the first instruction. It gets what the instruction is, and it sends it to the ALU.”，一致。5. 关键点6称“Alan Turing 表明，用六条原语——move left、move right、read、write、scan、do nothing——和一条纸带可以计算任何东西”，原文为“he showed that you can compute anything using the six primitives. And the six primitives are move left, move right, read, write, scan, and do nothing.”，一致。6. 关键点7称“Python 的原始构造包括 float、Boolean、数字、字符串和简单运算符（加、减等）”，原文为“There are floats, Booleans, these are numbers, strings, and simple operators, like addition, subtraction, and so on.”，一致。7. 关键点8称“静态语义错误在程序走到出错分支时也能被捕获”，原文为“Static semantic errors can also be caught by Python as long as, if your program has some decisions to make, as long as you've gone down the branch where the static semantic error happens.”，一致。8. 关键点10称“标量对象包括整数、浮点数、布尔值和 NoneType；布尔值只有 True 和 False（首字母大写），NoneType 只有 None，表示类型的缺失”，原文为“We have integers, for example, all of the whole numbers. Floats, which are all of the real numbers, anything with a decimal. Bools are Booleans. There's only two values to Booleans. That's True and False. Note the capitalization, capital T and capital F. And this other thing called NoneType. It's special. It has only one value called None. And it represents the absence of a type.”，一致。9. 关键点11称“在 shell 中输入 3 + 2 会显示值 5，但这只是程序员在查看值，不是真正打印”，原文为“If you're in the shell, if you simply type \\\"3 plus 2,\\\" you do see a value here. Five, right? But that's not actually printing something out.”，一致。10. 关键点12称“对 int 和 float，+、-、* 在两边都是整数时结果为整数，至少一边是浮点数时结果为浮点数；除法无论操作数是什么，结果总是浮点数”，原文为“If both of the variables of the operands are integers, then the result you're going to get is of type integer. But if at least one of them is a float, then the result you're going to get is a float. Division is a little bit special in that no matter what the operands are, the result is always going to be a float.”，一致。11. 关键点13称“编程与数学不同：右侧总是求值为值的表达式，左侧总是变量；要解 x，必须告诉计算机具体怎么算”，原文为“That means always in programming the right-hand side is going to be an expression. It's something that's going to be evaluated to a value. And the left-hand side is always a variable.”，一致。12. 关键点14称“area 的值没有改变，因为没有重新计算 area 的指令；只有执行重新计算 area 的指令才会改变它”，原文为“The value of area did not change. And it did not change because these are all the instructions we told the computer to do. We just told it to change radius to be radius plus 1. We never told it to recalculate the value of area.”，一致。13. 摘要称“MIT 6.0001/600 第一讲先介绍课程目标（概念、编程技能、通过 psets 解决问题）并强调练习”，原文确实提到“There's three big things we want to get out of this course. The first thing is the knowledge of concepts... The other thing we want you to get out of it is programming skills. And the last thing... is we teach you how to solve problems. And we do that through the psets.”，一致。14. 摘要称“讲座用陈述性知识与命令式知识、平方根算法、固定程序与存储程序架构、图灵原语等说明计算的基本原理”，原文均涉及，一致。15. 摘要称“并转入 Python 基础，介绍对象与类型、表达式与运算符、打印、赋值与内存绑定，以及程序单一含义与英语歧义的区别”，原文均涉及，一致。16. 摘要称“最后预告下一讲将加入控制流”，原文为“Next lecture, we're going to talk about adding control flow to our programs, so how do you tell the computer to do one thing or another?”，一致。未发现实质性不匹配。\"\n}",
